5. Feature Stack Construction
Script: src/offline/stack.py
Output: data/derived/stack_20m.tif
CRS: EPSG:32632 | Size: 1672×1669 | Bands: 25 | Resolution: 20 m

Band list:

#	Band	Source	Group
1	VV_mean	Sentinel-1 (ASC + DESC averaged)	Radar
2	VH_mean	Sentinel-1 (ASC + DESC averaged)	Radar
3	VV_std	Sentinel-1 (ASC + DESC averaged)	Radar
4	VH_std	Sentinel-1 (ASC + DESC averaged)	Radar
5	B02	Sentinel-2 median	Optical
6	B03	Sentinel-2 median	Optical
7	B04	Sentinel-2 median	Optical
8	B08	Sentinel-2 median	Optical
9	B11	Sentinel-2 median	Optical
10	B12	Sentinel-2 median	Optical
11	NDVI	Derived from B08 and B04	Optical
12	B11_B12_ratio	Derived from B11 and B12	Optical
13	elevation	Copernicus DEM GLO-30	Topographic
14	slope	Derived from elevation	Topographic
15	aspect_sin	Derived from elevation	Topographic
16	aspect_cos	Derived from elevation	Topographic
17	hillshade_000	Derived from elevation (azimuth 0°)	Topographic
18	hillshade_045	Derived from elevation (azimuth 45°)	Topographic
19	hillshade_090	Derived from elevation (azimuth 90°)	Topographic
20	hillshade_135	Derived from elevation (azimuth 135°)	Topographic
21	curvature	Laplacian of elevation	Topographic
22	tpi	Topographic Position Index (5×5 window)	Topographic
23	dist_road	Euclidean distance to OSM roads	Cultural
24	dist_waterway	Euclidean distance to OSM waterways	Cultural
25	builtup_fraction	Fraction of WorldCover class 50 per 20 m pixel	Cultural
6. Candidate Lineament Generation
Script: src/offline/candidates.py
Output: data/derived/candidates.geojson

6.1 Edge-detection inputs (7 sources)
Input	Source
hillshade_000	Stack band 17
hillshade_045	Stack band 18
hillshade_090	Stack band 19
hillshade_135	Stack band 20
VV_mean	Stack band 1
VH_mean	Stack band 2
S2_PC1	First principal component of Sentinel-2 bands (5–10)
6.2 Parameter sweep (4 configurations tested)
Setting	Vote threshold	Canny (low/high)	Segments	Mean length (m)
A (selected)	3	0.08 / 0.20	7,202	637.68
B	4	0.10 / 0.25	524	594.24
C	4	0.12 / 0.30	266	588.67
D	5	0.10 / 0.25	4	541.13
Selection rationale: Setting A is the only configuration producing a candidate count within the 2,000–8,000 target range specified in the Software Development Plan (Section 8.2).

6.3 Final selected parameters
Parameter	Value
Canny sigma	1.5
Canny low / high threshold	0.08 / 0.20
Vote threshold (of 7 inputs)	3
Hough min length	15 px (= 300 m)
Hough max gap	4 px (= 80 m)
Merge angle	10°
Merge gap	80 m
Minimum final length	500 m
6.4 Verification (scripts/verify_candidates.py)
Check	Target	Result	Status
Candidate count	2,000–8,000	7,202	✅ Pass
Minimum length	≥ 400 m	500 m	✅ Pass
Spatial extent	Within AOI	Within AOI	✅ Pass
CRS	EPSG:32632	EPSG:32632	✅ Pass
Spatial coverage	All bins	36 of 36 (100%)	✅ Pass
6.5 Azimuth distribution
Azimuth bin	Count
0–20°	478
20–40°	735
40–60°	1,338 (peak 1)
60–80°	588
80–100°	607
100–120°	732
120–140°	1,368 (peak 2)
140–160°	852
160–180°	504
Observation: Two dominant azimuth peaks at 40–60° and 120–140° — almost perpendicular to each other. Possible causes: (a) hillshade illumination bias, (b) Sentinel-1 look direction bias, (c) genuine NE–SW / NW–SE structural trend of the Niger Delta. Distinguishing these is the task of the Random Forest classifier.

